  STORE API
  ---------
  Store{New, ApplyBlock, Tip, RollbackTo, GetUTXO} wrapping *pgxpool.Pool. Checkpoint{Height,Hash} and UTXO{...} are the two small read-model types. No ORM/generic repository — every SQL/table-ordering concern stays inside internal/store (store.go, apply.go, reorg.go).

  ATOMIC BLOCK APPLY
  ------------------
  Transaction boundary: one pgx.Tx per ApplyBlock call (pool.Begin), passed to every helper; block header → per-tx body/variant/occurrence/inputs/witness/outputs/UTXO creation → per-tx UTXO spend marking → touched-address recompute → checkpoint.
  Checkpoint ordering: sync_state UPDATE is the last statement before Commit; only advances (block.Height >= current indexed_height), never rewinds; sync_state_validate_checkpoint_trigger independently re-verifies canonicality.
  Failure rollback: deferred tx.Rollback discards everything, including the block header row, on any error — proven by tests P/Q (mid-block failure leaves zero rows, zero checkpoint movement).

  IDEMPOTENCY
  -----------
  Replay behavior: every immutable write uses INSERT...ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING + verify-or-error (insertOrVerifyIdempotent); identical replay is a safe no-op; UTXO spend UPDATE...WHERE spent=false is idempotent for the exact same spender.
  Immutable conflict behavior: mismatched data for an already-stored identity (block hash/txid/wtxid/input/output/witness) returns ErrImmutableConflict, never a silent overwrite — proven by tests D, E, F.

  TXID / WTXID
  -------------
  Transaction body: transactions, keyed by txid, immutable non-witness body.
  Variant: transaction_variants, keyed by wtxid, size/vsize/weight.
  Witness: transaction_input_witness, keyed by (wtxid, vin_index, item_index) — two variants of the same txid (via rollback + replacement) remain independently queryable, proven by test I.

  UTXO
  ----
  Creation: utxo_state row inserted per output, creation_block_hash set, idempotent-verified on the creation identity only (never disturbs mutable spend fields).
  Spend: checkPrevout (read-only check) + markSpent (UPDATE...WHERE spent=false) — two-phase so UTXO FKs (transaction_inputs/block_transactions) exist before the spend UPDATE runs.
  Double-spend handling: ErrDoubleSpend, whole block rejected (test K).
  Missing-prevout handling: ErrMissingPrevout, whole block rejected (test L); store never invents a missing output.

  FEES
  ----
  Computation: sum(input values) - sum(output values), int64 satoshis only, ErrNegativeFee on inconsistency (test M).
  Coinbase: fee_satoshis unconditionally NULL (test N).

  ADDRESS CACHE
  -------------
  Recomputation method: recomputeAddress always SETs a fresh absolute aggregate from output_addresses/transaction_outputs/utxo_state (INSERT...ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE SET every column) — never an increment; deletes the row when zero remaining canonical activity.
  Multisig handling: output_participants never read by recomputeAddress — structurally cannot multiply a balance (test O).
  Replay result: cache after replay bit-for-bit equals cache before replay (tests C, R).

  REORG
  -----
  Rollback method: RollbackTo(ctx, ancestorHash) — one tx; finds all currently-canonical blocks above ancestor height (unique-per-height invariant makes this exactly the orphan set); no Core RPC involved, testable against synthetic persisted fork data.
  Immutable orphan history: blocks/transactions/transaction_variants/block_transactions/inputs/witness/outputs never deleted, only blocks.canonical flipped + orphaned_at set (test U).
  UTXO restoration: creations-only-in-orphan-range deleted; spends-only-in-orphan-range restored to unspent (tests S, T).
  Address restoration: every touched address recomputed from source tables; matches independent from-scratch aggregate after rollback+replacement (test X).
  Checkpoint: sync_state set to ancestor as final write, trigger re-verified (test V); replacement branch then applies normally via ordinary ApplyBlock (test W).

  P2QPK
  -----
  17,088-byte preservation: exact byte-for-byte round-trip through ApplyBlock into transaction_input_witness, confirmed by direct SQL readback (test H).
  Variant handling: P2QPK witness attached to a spending input is variant-scoped (wtxid-keyed) like any other witness, no special-casing needed.

